; The right button with no region sets the mark at point and point at
; the click, a temporary region; with one, it moves the nearer end to the
; click; a second click at the same place kills the region, as Emacs's
; mouse-save-then-kill does.
> (define (right! at . fields)
    (apply mouse! "down" at '("button" . 3) fields)
    (apply mouse! "click" at '("button" . 3) fields))
